       "w": 54.38,
       "text": "SLEEVE 1",
       "style": "tab"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "x": 74.13,
       "y": 6.75,
       "w": 383.13,
       "text": "To whoever is under this roof on the first of December.",
       "style": "addr"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "space",
     "h": 14
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p1",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The chute coughed once.",
       "span": "lead"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p2",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Iris looked up from a crate of brass number plates. Her cousin Pip had pinned the number eight to his sweater, although he had been told the pin was sharp."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p3",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "The chute coughed again, and a canvas bag hit the tiles hard enough to rattle every plate in the crate."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p4",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Pip got there first. “",
      {
       "text": "Now",
       "em": true
      },
      " can I investigate?”"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p5",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "“Hands where I can see them,” said their grandmother, Tessa Vale."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p6",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "She came around the table with the letter about the roof still in her hand. All morning it had moved between piles marked KEEP, GIVE AWAY and ASK SOMEONE."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p7",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Iris pointed the flashlight up the old parcel chute. The iron flap at the top was bolted. Dust furred the bolt, and a cobweb ran from it to the bricks."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p8",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "“Could have been a very thin postman,” said Pip."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p9",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Iris was twelve and liked an explanation to stay where she put it. Pip was eight and preferred one with room to crawl inside."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p10",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "The bag had twenty-four numbered pockets and a red 24 sewn by the handle. Tessa carried it to the table herself and stood over it with her back to them, longer than a bag needed. Then she locked the stair door."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p11",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "“The loft isn’t safe,” she said."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p12",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "“It was safe for carrying boxes ten minutes ago,” said Iris."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p13",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Under one buckle was a card, in the handwriting that was on every jar in the pantry and was not Grandma’s. ",
      {
       "text": "Alderwick Blind Route,",
       "em": true
      },
      " it said. ",
      {
       "text": "One sleeve a day, beginning on the first of December. No sleeve has a name on it. Figure out where it belongs and take it there. Curiosity does not count as postage.",
       "em": true
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "id": "d1-p14",
     "style": "story",
     "content": [
      "Pocket 1 held a paper sleeve. In it was a plan of the sorting rack on the far wall, and a line in the same hand: ",
      {
       "text": "Follow the mail.",
       "em": true
      }
     ]
    },
